# --- (b) the transfer conservation as polynomial identity in Z[t] ---------
# The Cayley rotation preserves |d|^2 iff c^2 + s^2 = 1 with
#   c = (1-t^2)/(1+t^2), s = 2t/(1+t^2).
# (1-t^2)^2 + (2t)^2 = (1+t^2)^2 as a POLYNOMIAL IDENTITY.
