# FIX LOG (V33d -> V33e):
#   [76] THE REPORTED CRASH: _arm_scaled used np.maximum(np.asarray(
#        tension - thr_), 0.0) on TRACED arrays inside the scan-traced
#        step -> TracerArrayConversionError (shape [2,32,32,32] = the
#        tension field). Introduced in the [75] cleanup pass; _arm_scaled
#        had never executed before Q3 (V33 is its first call site).
#        FIX: jnp.maximum(tension - thr_, 0.0) — pure JAX inside trace.
#   [77] _arm (dx-scaled) carried the SAME np.maximum pattern -> would
#        fire identically on any future re-run. Fixed identically.
#   [78] make_factory: THR/nu/dx captured constants normalized to
#        jnp.asarray AT CAPTURE (outside trace) — removes implicit
#        numpy->jnp coercion inside traced code.
#   [79] AUDITED-CLEAR: np.array(carry[0]) in run_dense is OUTSIDE the
#        trace (concrete snapshot) — not the crash source; the traceback
#        shape identifies the tension field, not the carry.
#   [80] gain arithmetic in _arm_scaled normalized to pure-jnp operand
#        chain (host scalars legal; traced operands must stay jnp).
#   BOUNDARY RULE NOW ENFORCED LINE-BY-LINE: inside traced functions,
#   every array op is jnp.*; numpy touches only host constants and
